t2_waived: "A design run decides how a screen will look and changes no user-observable contract, so there is no T2 fact to synthesise yet: UC-4's surface gains the export, import and clear controls when W6 BUILDS them, and stating them now would put a capability in the use-case KB that the app does not have. The rulebook is untouched for the same reason plus a specific one — the only T2 write-back this line of work owed was run 10's Lexicon question, and W5 already landed it, so `export` has its row and this run inherits it rather than proposing a term. The run's THREE proposals - promote ModalShell as Dialog, three IconButton glyph entries, and a new rulebook soft rule (safe-answer-takes-focus: a destructive ask focuses the answer that does nothing) - are recorded in the run's Proposals list and belong to their owners; a run proposes and an owner performs, so none is a T2 edit this WU may make. The third is the one a reader should notice: the rulebook has no rule on destructive focus at all, this run had to derive it from a Frame constraint and got it wrong on the first pass, and the rulebook's own growth mechanism says a design needing a rule that is not there proposes it. Proposing it is therefore the T2 obligation this WU discharges - by recording it, not by writing the row."
